'''Pat Matson''' (July 22, 1944 – September 8, 2025<ref>[https://www.packers.com/news/former-packers-ol-pat-matson-died-at-81 Former Packers OL Pat Matson died at 81]</ref>) was an [[American Football League]] and [[National Football League]] [[offensive lineman]]. He played for the [[Denver Broncos]] (1966–1967), the [[Cincinnati Bengals]] (1968–1974), and the [[Green Bay Packers]] (1975). He played college football at [[University of Oregon]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pat Matson |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MatsPa20.htm |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221006204351/https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MatsPa20.htm |archive-date=2022-10-06 |access-date=2023-04-23 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-world/163605942/ | title=Burly Pat Matson, 'Refugee' Fill Tackles Slots For Oregon Gridders | work=[[The World (Coos Bay, Oregon)|The World]] | date=August 18, 1965 | accessdate=21 January 2025}}</ref>
